<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Create Boundary From Mapping" boundary tool (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormBndTool`
    (FormBndTool.cs + FormBndTool.Designer.cs) — the LARGEST Field dialog. The operator
    builds a field boundary from recorded section/coverage points: choose a point spacing
    and smoothing, reduce / add points, run the build, slice, then save the result. The
    dialog hosts a live OpenGL viewport on the LEFT and a touch-friendly command panel on
    the RIGHT, with a "Please Wait" progress overlay shown while the build runs. Per AAP
    §0.3.3 this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the current Windows Forms look,
    never a redesign: no new colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormBndTool.Designer.cs:
      Text "Create Boundary From Mapping" → Title (design-time placeholder; the code-behind
                                             assigns the localised gStr text at runtime).
      ClientSize 1006 x 726 / MinimumSize 1022 x 742 → initial Width/Height + MinWidth/MinHeight.
                                             The code-behind applies the persisted
                                             Settings.setWindow_MapBndSize on load and saves it
                                             on close, so the window is resizable.
      Resizable WinForms form              → CanResize="True" (honour the persisted size).
      ShowInTaskbar = false                → ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition CenterParent           → WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
      BackColor (LightGray)                → Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}". Per the
                                             file spec the neutral chrome is themed to App.axaml's
                                             day/night palette rather than hard-coding a WinForms
                                             colour (reference with DynamicResource so the live
                                             Light↔Dark switch is observed).
      Font Tahoma                          → FontFamily="Tahoma"; children carry their own point
                                             sizes converted to Avalonia DIP (pt × 96 / 72):
                                             27.75 → 37, 15.75 → 21, 14.25 → 19, 12 → 16, 36 → 48.

    GL HOSTING (markup side only) — CRITICAL:
      The WinForms `oglSelf` (OpenTK.GLControl) surface is REPLACED by an empty Border named
      `oglHost`. There is NO OpenTK.GLControl in Avalonia and this markup must NOT instantiate
      `AvaloniaGeoViewport` nor reference the `AgOpenGPS.Controls` namespace. The partner
      code-behind (FormBndToolView.axaml.cs) constructs the AvaloniaGeoViewport with the field
      bounding box and inserts its exposed Control as `oglHost.Child`; it also wires pointer /
      wheel forwarding — so NO input bindings are declared here.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind owns ALL behaviour:
      * Code-behind dialog: NO DataContext, NO x:DataType, NO MVVM bindings (exactly like the
        sibling FormPanView / FormShiftPosView). Every control is addressed imperatively by its
        x:Name, which keeps the ORIGINAL WinForms name so the migrated code-behind references it
        exactly as FormBndTool.cs / .Designer.cs did.
      * NO Click= / event attributes are declared here on purpose: the handler method names are
        owned by the code-behind, which subscribes by name (e.g. btnExit.Click += ...) using the
        named fields below. This keeps the view compiling independently of the code-behind.
      * Design-time defaults reproduced from the designer: cboxPointDistance / cboxSmooth carry
        their static item lists (code-behind sets SelectedIndex from Settings.bndToolSpacing /
        bndToolSmooth); btnStartStop / btnAddPoints start IsEnabled="False"; labelSpacing starts
        IsEnabled="False"; panel1 (the progress overlay) starts IsVisible="False" — all toggled
        by the code-behind. Every button glyph is STATIC (the WinForms code-behind never swaps a
        Button.Image), so each Source is set here.
      * Label captions ("Spacing (m)", "Smooth", "Reset", "Add Points", "Please Wait",
        "Points to Process: ", "Points:") are design-time placeholders; the code-behind localises
        them via gStr on load.

    Button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs,
    the convention used by every sibling GPS view; note btnImages/Config/ConS_SourceFix.png lives
    in a sub-folder and back-button.png uses a hyphen (verified against Properties/Resources.resx).
    No WinForms, no OpenTK, no GMap, no System.Drawing types are referenced. Avalonia 11.3.x.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormBndToolView"
        Title="Create Boundary From Mapping"
        Width="1022"
        Height="742"
        MinWidth="1022"
        MinHeight="742"
        CanResize="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <!--
        Tool-button style (Classes="tool"): the command-panel buttons keep the STANDARD (themed)
        Fluent button face, reproducing the WinForms light tiles (FlatStyle.Flat with White /
        WhiteSmoke BackColor) while remaining day/night aware. Padding is tightened and the button
        stretches to fill its grid cell so the centred glyph dominates, matching the WinForms
        buttons that filled their TableLayoutPanel cells. The :disabled rule dims the glyph (an
        Avalonia <Image> is not affected by the Fluent disabled foreground), reproducing the greyed
        look of the initially-disabled btnStartStop / btnAddPoints.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.tool">
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="3" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="2" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Stretch" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.tool:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Two-column shell (replaces the WinForms absolute layout of oglSelf + tlp1 + panel1):
          Column 0 (star)  → the GL viewport host, filling the main render area.
          Column 1 (fixed) → the command panel (the WinForms tlp1 was ~299 px wide).
        The "Please Wait" overlay (panel1) shares Column 0 and is drawn AFTER oglHost so it sits
        on top of the viewport, exactly as the WinForms panel1 floated over oglSelf.
    -->
    <Grid>
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
            <ColumnDefinition Width="340" />
        </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

        <!-- GL viewport host. REPLACES the WinForms oglSelf (OpenTK.GLControl, BackColor Black).
             Intentionally EMPTY: the code-behind sets oglHost.Child = _viewport.View. The Black
             background shows until the renderer paints its first frame. -->
        <Border x:Name="oglHost"
                Grid.Column="0"
                Background="Black" />

        <!-- panel1: the "Please Wait" progress overlay. WinForms BackColor MistyRose (#FFFFE4E1),
             starts hidden (FormBndTool_Load) and is shown by the code-behind while the build runs.
             Centred over the GL area; the fixed light alert colour keeps black text legible, so the
             inner labels hard-code Foreground="Black" (parity — this panel is not themed). -->
        <Border x:Name="panel1"
                Grid.Column="0"
                IsVisible="False"
                Background="#FFFFE4E1"
                Width="445"
                Height="305"
                HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Vertical"
                        Spacing="14"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <!-- labelPleaseWait: "Please Wait" (runtime: gStr.gsPleaseWait + "..."). 15.75pt → 21. -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="labelPleaseWait"
                           Text="Please Wait"
                           FontSize="21"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                <!-- "Points to Process: " caption + live count (lblPointToProcess). -->
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="labelPointsToProcess"
                               Text="Points to Process: "
                               FontSize="21"
                               Foreground="Black"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="lblPointToProcess"
                               Text="100,000"
                               FontSize="21"
                               FontWeight="Bold"
                               Foreground="Black"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </StackPanel>
                <!-- "Points:" caption + live count (lblI). -->
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="labelPoints"
                               Text="Points:"
                               FontSize="21"
                               Foreground="Black"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="lblI"
                               Text="Points"
                               FontSize="21"
                               FontWeight="Bold"
                               Foreground="Black"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </StackPanel>
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <!--
            Command panel — replaces the WinForms tlp1 TableLayoutPanel (6 columns × 10 rows).
            The column / row proportions are reproduced exactly as fractional star weights (the
            WinForms ColumnStyle / RowStyle percentages); rows 5 and 9 were Absolute (21 px, 79 px).
            Columns 1 and 4 are the thin spacer columns. This panel is intentionally UNNAMED (the
            migrated code-behind relies on Avalonia auto-layout, not the WinForms tlp1 field).
        -->
        <Grid Grid.Column="1" Margin="6">
            <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <ColumnDefinition Width="25.83893*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="2.684564*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="23.15436*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="23.15436*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="2.684564*" />
                <ColumnDefinition Width="22.48323*" />
            </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
            <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <RowDefinition Height="12.00456*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="5.506683*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="15.71025*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="4.003683*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="13.8699*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="21" />
                <RowDefinition Height="20.21404*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="14.8345*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="13.8564*" />
                <RowDefinition Height="79" />
            </Grid.RowDefinitions>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 0 — spacing / smooth selectors ============================ -->

            <!-- cboxPointDistance: point-spacing selector (left group, cols 0-2). Items 1..10 + "?";
                 code-behind sets SelectedIndex = Settings.bndToolSpacing. 27.75pt → 37 DIP Bold. -->
            <ComboBox x:Name="cboxPointDistance"
                      Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                      Margin="3"
                      HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                      VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                      FontSize="37"
                      FontWeight="Bold"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Point spacing">
                <ComboBoxItem>1</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>2</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>3</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>4</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>5</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>6</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>7</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>8</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>9</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>10</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>?</ComboBoxItem>
            </ComboBox>

            <!-- cboxSmooth: smoothing-passes selector (right group, cols 3-5). Items 0/4/8/16/32/64 + "?";
                 code-behind sets SelectedIndex = Settings.bndToolSmooth. 27.75pt → 37 DIP Bold. -->
            <ComboBox x:Name="cboxSmooth"
                      Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                      Margin="3"
                      HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                      VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                      FontSize="37"
                      FontWeight="Bold"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Smoothing">
                <ComboBoxItem>0</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>4</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>8</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>16</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>32</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>64</ComboBoxItem>
                <ComboBoxItem>?</ComboBoxItem>
            </ComboBox>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 1 — selector captions ============================ -->

            <!-- labelSpacing: "Spacing (m)" (runtime: "{gsSpacing} ({gsCm})"). Designer Enabled=false. 12pt → 16. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelSpacing"
                       Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Spacing (m)"
                       FontSize="16"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       IsEnabled="False"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- labelSmooth: "Smooth" (runtime gStr.gsSmooth). 12pt → 16. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelSmooth"
                       Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Smooth"
                       FontSize="16"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- ============================ ROW 2 — reset / add points ============================ -->

            <!-- btnResetReduce: reset / step-back the reduction (glyph back-button.png). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnResetReduce"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Reset / reduce">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/back-button.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- btnAddPoints: add interpolated points (glyph PointAdd.png). Designer Enabled=false. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnAddPoints"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Add points">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/PointAdd.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 3 — action captions ============================ -->

            <!-- labelReset: "Reset". 12pt → 16. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelReset"
                       Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="3" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Reset"
                       FontSize="16"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- labelCreate: "Add Points" (runtime gStr.gsCreate). 12pt → 16. -->
            <TextBlock x:Name="labelCreate"
                       Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="3" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Add Points"
                       FontSize="16"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- ============================ ROW 4 — start/stop build / add boundary ============================ -->

            <!-- btnStartStop: start / stop the reduce build (glyph BoundaryReduce.png). Designer Enabled=false. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnStartStop"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="4" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    IsEnabled="False"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Start / stop build">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/BoundaryReduce.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- btnAddBoundary: add the outer boundary (glyph BoundaryOuter.png). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnAddBoundary"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="4" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Add boundary">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/BoundaryOuter.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 5 — group captions (Build / Save) ============================ -->
            <!-- WinForms label3 / label2: static section captions, NOT referenced by the code-behind,
                 so left UNNAMED to avoid duplicating a code-behind field. 12pt → 16. -->
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="5" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Build"
                       FontSize="16"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />

            <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="5" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                       Text="Save"
                       FontSize="16"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       TextAlignment="Center" />

            <!-- ============================ ROW 6 — cancel touch / slice ============================ -->

            <!-- btnCancelTouch: cancel / delete touched points (glyph HeadlandDeletePoints.png). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnCancelTouch"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="6" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel / delete points">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/HeadlandDeletePoints.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- btnSlice: slice / make line (glyph BoundaryMakeLine.png). Code-behind toggles visibility. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnSlice"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="6" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Slice / make line">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/BoundaryMakeLine.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 7 — center view / zoom toggle ============================ -->

            <!-- btnCenterOGL: recenter the viewport (glyph Config/ConS_SourceFix.png — sub-folder asset). -->
            <Button x:Name="btnCenterOGL"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="7" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Center view">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Config/ConS_SourceFix.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- cboxIsZoom: a CheckBox styled as a toggle button (WinForms Appearance=Button). Retemplated
                 as a Border + centred ContentPresenter holding the ZoomOGL glyph; the :checked state swaps
                 the fill to the WinForms FlatAppearance.CheckedBackColor #FFB4FFA0 (FromArgb(180,255,160)).
                 The border uses the themed text brush so it reads in day and night. -->
            <CheckBox x:Name="cboxIsZoom"
                      Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="7" Grid.ColumnSpan="3"
                      Margin="3"
                      HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                      VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                      HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                      VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                      AutomationProperties.Name="Zoom to extent">
                <CheckBox.Template>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="CheckBox">
                        <Border x:Name="zoomBorder"
                                Background="Transparent"
                                BorderBrush="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="1">
                            <ContentPresenter Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                              HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                                              VerticalContentAlignment="Center" />
                        </Border>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </CheckBox.Template>
                <CheckBox.Styles>
                    <Style Selector="CheckBox:checked /template/ Border#zoomBorder">
                        <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFB4FFA0" />
                    </Style>
                </CheckBox.Styles>
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ZoomOGL.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="6" />
            </CheckBox>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 8 — pan move buttons ============================ -->
            <!-- WinForms places the four move buttons across one row at cols 0 / 2 / 3 / 5
                 (cols 1 and 4 are the thin spacers): Down, Up, Left, Right. -->

            <Button x:Name="btnMoveDn"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="8"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Move down">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/DnArrow64.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <Button x:Name="btnMoveUp"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="2" Grid.Row="8"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Move up">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/UpArrow64.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <Button x:Name="btnMoveLeft"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="3" Grid.Row="8"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Move left">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ArrowLeft.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <Button x:Name="btnMoveRight"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="5" Grid.Row="8"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Move right">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ArrowRight.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

            <!-- ============================ ROW 9 — zoom out / zoom in / exit ============================ -->

            <!-- btnZoomOut: "-" zoom out. 36pt → 48 DIP Bold. Spans cols 0-1. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnZoomOut"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="0" Grid.Row="9" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                    Content="-"
                    FontSize="48"
                    FontWeight="Bold"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Zoom out" />

            <!-- btnZoomIn: "+" zoom in. 27.75pt → 37 DIP Bold. Spans cols 2-3. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnZoomIn"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="2" Grid.Row="9" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                    Content="+"
                    FontSize="37"
                    FontWeight="Bold"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Zoom in" />

            <!-- btnExit: accept / close (glyph OK64.png; WinForms DialogResult.Cancel). Spans cols 4-5.
                 IsDefault routes Enter to this button for keyboard operability. -->
            <Button x:Name="btnExit"
                    Classes="tool"
                    Grid.Column="4" Grid.Row="9" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                    IsDefault="True"
                    AutomationProperties.Name="Exit">
                <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                       Stretch="Uniform" Margin="4" />
            </Button>

        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
